1. Work performed

Persistent attention metadata now lives on the slice instead of being recreated on every `Run()`. In [attention_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_layer.cpp:26) `DeviceBuffer::CopyFromHost()` no longer does a device sync, and [attention_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_layer.cpp:379) adds slice-owned metadata scratch for `seq_len_q`, `seq_len_kv`, `query_starts`, `page_table_k`, and `page_table_v`. In [attention_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_layer.cpp:595) `Run()` now reuses a persistent host/device metadata plan and updates only the active metadata with `cudaMemcpyAsync` before the scatter/attention launches.

2. Sync points removed

Removed unconditional `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` from the attention fallback helpers in [attention_device_fallback.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_device_fallback.cu:208), [attention_device_fallback.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_device_fallback.cu:237), [attention_device_fallback.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_device_fallback.cu:274), and [attention_device_fallback.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_device_fallback.cu:337). Removed the per-launch host syncs from [fused_mamba_decode.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/fused_mamba_decode.cu:171) and [fused_moe_decode.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/fused_moe_decode.cu:314).

3. Compile status

`nemotron_runtime_backend` built successfully. `full_forward_manifest_smoke_test` built successfully. I did not run the runtime correctness or benchmark commands in this turn.

4. Concerns

The page-table buffers are persistent, but their full max-page sizing is established lazily on first use from `request_context.config().max_tokens`; after that the steady-state path is allocation-free. Also, cuDNN attention plan/workspace creation is still per-call, so this checkpoint removes the metadata malloc/sync overhead but does not yet address cuDNN plan lifetime.

CHECKPOINT: 3
